cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EasyCellCounting: fast, reproducible counting of fluorescent cells in microscopy images"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Khambete
    given-names: Amav
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ack41704/EasyCellCounting"
keywords:
  - cell counting
  - fluorescence microscopy
  - image analysis
  - tdTomato
  - neuroscience
abstract: >-
  Semi-automated counting of bright fluorescent cells on the left and right side
  of a region of interest. Regions are drawn interactively on screen-sized previews
  and counted in batch at full resolution by thresholding, contour segmentation,
  area-based single-cell / cluster classification and a cluster-to-cell estimate
  from the single-cell area distribution of the same region.
